<div class="rg-grid">
  <div class="rg-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Resource governance</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Put predictable limits on large files.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      DOCX, XLSX and PPTX share measured package-expansion limits. The defaults allow
      <strong>128 MiB per part</strong> and <strong>256 MiB across distinct parts read</strong>
      during a package session. Crossing a limit rejects with a structured
      <code>OoxmlResourceLimitError</code> before that measured condition is left to an
      opaque browser crash.
    </p>
    <div class="rg-facts">
      <div>
        <strong>Calibrate with real traffic</strong>
        <span><code>onResourceMetrics</code> captures the initial load independently of debug logging; <code>getResourceMetrics()</code> returns a fresh snapshot after lazy package access.</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Inspect without instrumentation</strong>
        <span><code>debug: true</code> prints the same report as one aligned console card. The library never transmits or stores it.</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <strong>Choose stronger containment</strong>
        <span><code>mode: 'worker'</code> keeps parser and renderer state away from Window. It is opt-in and is not an operating-system process or a strict memory sandbox.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="rg-caveat">
      Raster decode is also guarded uniformly: 32 MP per image, 128 MiB of decoded
      ownership per document cache or render pass, and two concurrent decodes. These are
      deterministic admission guards—not exact JavaScript, WASM, canvas or GPU accounting—so
      they reduce catastrophic-failure risk but cannot guarantee that every device avoids OOM.
      Browser-managed SVG/vector storage has no portable decoded-byte metric; its cache is
      count-bounded and owned object URLs are revoked, but it is outside the RGBA counter.
    </p>
  </div>

  <pre class="rg-code"><code><span class="kw">const</span> viewer = <span class="kw">new</span> DocxViewer(canvas, {'{'}
  resourceLimits: {'{'}
    maxArchiveEntryBytes: <span class="num">128</span> * <span class="num">1024</span> * <span class="num">1024</span>,
    maxTotalInflatedBytes: <span class="num">256</span> * <span class="num">1024</span> * <span class="num">1024</span>,
  {'}'},
  onResourceMetrics(metrics) {'{'}
    analytics.record(<span class="str">'ooxml-resource-usage'</span>, metrics);
  {'}'},
  <span class="cm">// debug: true, // local or staging inspection</span>
  <span class="cm">// mode: 'worker', // optional stronger containment</span>
{'}'});</code></pre>
</div>

